# Mutation plan for every GET in api4/group.go — ten routes, twelve paths, one answer.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/groups.plan
#
# `requireLicense` (api4/handlers.go:237) is the **generic** licence error — one id, one status,
# shared by every group route — where the three channel gates each have their own and two of them
# answer 403. So the mutations here are: the status, the id, the blank `where`, and forwarding a
# licensed installation rather than answering it.
#
# **A mutation of the blank `where` was written and then dropped.** `AppError.Where` carries
# `json:"-"` in Go and `#[serde(skip)]` here, so it is on nobody's wire and no parity test can see
# it — it survived, as it had to. That Go leaves it blank on purpose (handlers.go:239) where every
# other error in the tree names its caller is recorded in the module doc instead, which is where a
# reader changing the line will look.
#
# **The eight routes added later are all the same `answer`**, so the three mutations above already
# cover their bodies. What is *not* shared is the routing, and that is where the new lines go: the
# `teams|channels` alternation, and the literal siblings that must not be read as syncable types.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.

